Section 4(f)(5)
FHWA should only be contacted if publicly-owned parks, recreation areas, and wildlife and waterfowl refuges have
been identified in the project area. Section 4(f) concerns with historic resources should be addressed through the
Cultural Resource Agency Coordination Meetings.
